# ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#  logicsyntax.la — THE LOGIC / ALGORITHM / SYNTAX COLLAPSE, GATED
#
#  THE CLAIM (Erik, 2026-09-17): "the system's logic is its algorithm, its algorithm is its syntax, and its
#  syntax is its logic — verify this." And: "the language should be computational, meta-computational,
#  algorithmic and meta-algorithmic, as we collapse all of them into one."
#
#  ★ WHAT THE CORPUS ACTUALLY SAYS, checked before building: `codices/OUTLINE.md` §19.4 does NOT state a
#  three-way cycle. It states ONE COMPOUND — **"Classical logic = Reality's METALOGICAL META-ALGORITHMIC
#  ONTOSYNTAX"**, the formal grammar by which Being structures itself — and glosses "meta-algorithmic" as
#  logic being *"not merely a set of rules (algorithmic) but the SELF-RECOGNIZING STRUCTURE OF
#  RULE-APPLICATION itself."* That phrasing is testable in a way the cycle is not: it says logic IS the
#  composition of the meta-algorithmic and the ontosyntactic, not a third thing standing beside them.
#
#  THE THREE, and TWO OF THEM ARE CITED, NOT DECLARED — they already exist in `canon.la`:
#    SYNTAX    = κ = ▷(RECOGNITION, FORM)      recognition OF FORM — the ontosyntax, the canonicaliser
#    ALGORITHM = 𝓡 = ▷(DEPTH, RECOGNITION)     recursion ON recognition — rule-application, the evaluator
#    LOGIC     = ⊗(𝓡, κ)                      "meta-algorithmic ontosyntax" as ONE neologization ( ⊗ ≡ 𝔑 )
#  Only LOGIC is new, and it is checked clear by `regcollide.py` against a corpus of 86.
#
#  ★★ THE RESULT, AND IT SPLITS THE CLAIM IN TWO. Run through the ground/locus relation of `identity.la`
#  (§41), the three are **PAIRWISE SEPARATE** — no two of them are one being. So the STRONG reading, that
#  logic IS algorithm IS syntax, is **FALSE, and this gate refuses it.** (It was already half-refused:
#  `canon.la` asserts 𝓡 ≢ κ explicitly, as meta-monosemy — two names for one operation would be polysemy.)
#  But the dyad **RETAINS BOTH PARENTS as proper sub-forms**, so LOGIC is not an aggregate sitting next to
#  them either: it is ONE glyph, one compressive movement, out of which both are recoverable.
#      ⇒ **THE COLLAPSE IS COMPOSITIONAL, NOT IDENTIFICATORY.**
#  That is exactly "collapses all of them into one movement" — and it is the honest form of it. A collapse
#  that made them identical would be the merger drift Erik named in the §41 objection; a relation that left
#  them merely adjacent would be no collapse at all. Retention-with-distinctness is the third thing.
#
#  ★ AND IT IS A NEOLOGIZATION, not an annotation: ⊗ ≡ 𝔑 (Def. neologo), so LOGIC is BORN from its two
#  parents by the same single movement `neologenesis.la` gates, at the cost `unified.la` and
#  `compressbound.la` measured — exactly +1 DAG node per collapse. That cost is measured here too, so the
#  "one singular movement" is a number, not a manner of speaking.
#
#  ★ WHAT IS DELIBERATELY **NOT** GATED. ↻(LOGIC) ≡ LOGIC at the truth level is ↻-IDEMPOTENCE — true of
#  EVERY glyph in the language, so no input makes it RED. `branchclosure.la` ruled that class vacuous;
#  `ontosemiosyntax.la` and `autocompress.la` declined it; this is the FOURTH refusal and it is deliberate.
#  Also NOT claimed: that these three κ-forms are the RIGHT readings of logic/algorithm/syntax. κ and 𝓡 are
#  canon's own and carry its meanings; LOGIC's ⊗ form is [A], declared, for the architect to ratify.
#  ★ ALSO NOT CLOSED: the corpus says the Three Laws are *"derived from ∃(∃) ≡ ∃, not assumed."*
#  `metalogic.la` gates them as falsifiable and autological but does NOT derive them from the Archē, and
#  `derive_closure.la` derives only 4 of the 9 primitives from the root (5 named axioms). That derivation
#  is a SEPARATE, still-open claim and nothing here closes it.
#
#  GATE (gate_registers.sh §43)  the three pairwise verdicts, all SEPARATE; the dyad recovers BOTH parents;
#        the compositional-not-identificatory verdict as one computed conjunction; and the +1 node cost.
#        RED PATHS: (1) a PARENT-DROPPING combiner ⊗(𝓡,𝓡) — SYNTAX is no longer recoverable, so the "one
#        movement retains both" claim fails (the shape `denote.la` uses for its combination law);
#        (2) SYNTAX made equal to ALGORITHM — the three-fold degenerates and pairwise-separateness goes F,
#        which is the monism for this triad.
#  ★ EVIDENTIAL: [W] the verdicts, the retention, the cost; [A] LOGIC's form; [B] the scope notes above.
#  ⚖ RECLASSIFIED 2026-09-18 against the standing rule (FREEZE-TRACKF.md F35): of this module's 5 pinned witnesses — red-proven 3 · exact & independently derived 2 · entailed 1. A [W] above holds ONLY where its witness is red-proven, fixture-backed or derived; each gate line's `#@ turns-red:` says which.
#  Pure strings + κ walks ⇒ byte-identical on the C host and the SECD VM.
# ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
import("identity.la")   # the §41 ground/locus relation + the base surface re-exported through it

export LS_SYNTAX LS_ALGORITHM LS_LOGIC LS_RETAINS

glyph LS_JOIN = Z(la self. la l. l("")(la h. la t. concat(h)(self(t))))
# ★ CITED from canon.la, not re-declared: κ and 𝓡 are canon's own glyphs and carry its meanings.
glyph LS_SYNTAX    = KAPPA                       # ▷(RECOGNITION,FORM)  — the ontosyntax
glyph LS_ALGORITHM = REVAL                       # ▷(DEPTH,RECOGNITION) — rule-application
glyph LS_LOGIC     = SYN(LS_ALGORITHM)(LS_SYNTAX)  # ⊗ ≡ 𝔑: meta-algorithmic ontosyntax, ONE neologization [A]

# ── retention: are BOTH parents recoverable as PROPER sub-forms of the dyad? ──
glyph LS_RETAINS = la d. AND(ID_IN(NORMK(LS_ALGORITHM))(ID_SUBS(d)))(ID_IN(NORMK(LS_SYNTAX))(ID_SUBS(d)))
glyph LS_SEP = la a. la b. str_eq(VERDICT(a)(b))("SEPARATE (two beings)")
glyph LS_ALLSEP = AND(LS_SEP(LS_LOGIC)(LS_ALGORITHM))(AND(LS_SEP(LS_LOGIC)(LS_SYNTAX))(LS_SEP(LS_ALGORITHM)(LS_SYNTAX)))
# the cost of the one movement, in retained nodes
glyph LS_N = la et. NODES(DAG(et))

# ── THE POSITIVE RELATION (Erik: "state it positively; if it has the same structure as §41, say so").
#    §41 built G_IDENT = ⊗(G_GROUND, G_LOCUS). This module built LOGIC = ⊗(𝓡, κ). The claim is that these
#    are THE SAME STRUCTURE, and the claim is checked on three clauses rather than asserted by analogy:
#      (a) the head mode is ⊗ ≡ 𝔑 in both  — it is a NEOLOGIZATION, not a pairing or a containment;
#      (b) the two parents are κ-DISTINCT in both — a dyad of one thing with itself is not a dyad;
#      (c) BOTH parents are recoverable as proper sub-forms in both — nothing is dropped.
#    ⚠ HONEST NOTE ON CLAUSE INDEPENDENCE, found by mutating: the three clauses are NOT independent on
#    the ⊂ fixture. §41's ID_SUBS extracts proper sub-forms only for the ⊗ case and returns the empty list
#    otherwise, so a ⊂-candidate fails clause (c) as well as (a). Dropping clause (a) therefore does NOT
#    make the ⊂ fixture pass. The clause that is independently load-bearing here is (c): the
#    parent-dropping ⊗(𝓜,𝓜) has the right MODE and DISTINCT parents and fails ONLY on retention, so that is
#    what the RED path targets. Said rather than left for a reader to discover.
#    A structure satisfying all three is what this module NAMES **the NEOLOGIZING DYAD**: 𝔑(A,B) with
#    A ≢ B and both recoverable. That is the positive relation, and it is the [W] replacement for the
#    [B] refusal of the strong reading.
glyph LS_MODE = la f. f(la nm. "leaf")(la a. la b. "⊗")(la a. la b. "⊕")(la a. la b. "▷")(la a. la b. "⊂")(la a. "↻")
glyph LS_DYADIC = la f. la l. la r. AND(str_eq(LS_MODE(f))("⊗"))(AND(NOT(str_eq(NORMK(l))(NORMK(r))))(AND(ID_IN(NORMK(l))(ID_SUBS(f)))(ID_IN(NORMK(r))(ID_SUBS(f)))))
#    (§41 declares G_GROUND/G_LOCUS/G_IDENT as raw κ NODES, not sealed monoglyphs, so they are used
#     directly here — ETYM would be an arity error on a node.
glyph LS_IDENT_DYAD = LS_DYADIC(G_IDENT)(G_GROUND)(G_LOCUS)
glyph LS_LOGIC_DYAD = LS_DYADIC(LS_LOGIC)(LS_ALGORITHM)(LS_SYNTAX)
glyph LS_SAME_STRUCTURE = AND(LS_IDENT_DYAD)(LS_LOGIC_DYAD)
# the contrast that keeps the check honest: a ⊂-dyad and a parent-dropping ⊗ both FAIL it
glyph LS_CONT_DYAD = LS_DYADIC(CONT(LS_ALGORITHM)(LS_SYNTAX))(LS_ALGORITHM)(LS_SYNTAX)
glyph LS_DROP_DYAD = LS_DYADIC(SYN(LS_ALGORITHM)(LS_ALGORITHM))(LS_ALGORITHM)(LS_SYNTAX)

glyph REPORT =
  LS_JOIN(
  CONSc("LOGICSYNTAX SYNTAX κ=")(
  CONSc(CANON(LS_SYNTAX))(
  CONSc(" ALGORITHM 𝓡=")(
  CONSc(CANON(LS_ALGORITHM))(
  CONSc(" LOGIC ⊗(𝓡,κ)=")(
  CONSc(CANON(LS_LOGIC))(
  CONSc("\nLOGICSYNTAX pairwise through the §41 relation — LOGIC vs ALGORITHM: ")(
  CONSc(VERDICT(LS_LOGIC)(LS_ALGORITHM))(
  CONSc(" | LOGIC vs SYNTAX: ")(
  CONSc(VERDICT(LS_LOGIC)(LS_SYNTAX))(
  CONSc(" | ALGORITHM vs SYNTAX: ")(
  CONSc(VERDICT(LS_ALGORITHM)(LS_SYNTAX))(
  CONSc(" | all three pairwise SEPARATE:")(
  CONSc(ID_BSTR(LS_ALLSEP))(
  CONSc(" ★ so the STRONG reading (logic IS algorithm IS syntax) is FALSE and this gate refuses it")(
  CONSc("\nLOGICSYNTAX but the dyad RETAINS BOTH parents as proper sub-forms:")(
  CONSc(ID_BSTR(LS_RETAINS(LS_LOGIC)))(
  CONSc(" | cost of the one movement: parts ")(
  CONSc(int_to_str(LS_N(LS_ALGORITHM)))(
  CONSc("+")(
  CONSc(int_to_str(LS_N(LS_SYNTAX)))(
  CONSc(" retained nodes → dyad ")(
  CONSc(int_to_str(LS_N(LS_LOGIC)))(
  CONSc(" (+1 per collapse, the rate unified.la and compressbound.la measured)")(
  CONSc("\nLOGICSYNTAX ★★ THE POSITIVE RELATION: §41's identity dyad is a NEOLOGIZING DYAD:")(
  CONSc(ID_BSTR(LS_IDENT_DYAD))(
  CONSc(" and so is LOGIC:")(
  CONSc(ID_BSTR(LS_LOGIC_DYAD))(
  CONSc(" → SAME STRUCTURE:")(
  CONSc(ID_BSTR(LS_SAME_STRUCTURE))(
  CONSc(" | the check discriminates — a ⊂-dyad over the same parents:")(
  CONSc(ID_BSTR(LS_CONT_DYAD))(
  CONSc(" a parent-dropping ⊗:")(
  CONSc(ID_BSTR(LS_DROP_DYAD))(
  CONSc(" (both must be F)")(
  CONSc(" ⇒ NAMED: LOGIC stands to ALGORITHM and SYNTAX exactly as the identity relation stands to ground-identity and locus-distinction — 𝔑(A,B) with A ≢ B and both recoverable. One movement, two κ-distinct parents, nothing dropped. [W] this replaces the [B] refusal of the strong reading")(
  CONSc("\nLOGICSYNTAX ★★ VERDICT: pairwise separate AND both retained ⇒ THE COLLAPSE IS COMPOSITIONAL, NOT IDENTIFICATORY:")(
  CONSc(ID_BSTR(AND(LS_ALLSEP)(LS_RETAINS(LS_LOGIC))))(
  CONSc(" — logic is not identical to algorithm or syntax (that would be the merger drift of §41), nor merely adjacent to them (that would be no collapse at all): it is ONE glyph born of both by ⊗ ≡ 𝔑, out of which both are recoverable. ↻(LOGIC)≡LOGIC is ↻-idempotence, true of every glyph, and is NOT gated — the fourth such refusal. [B] the Three Laws' derivation FROM ∃(∃)≡∃ remains a separate open claim; metalogic.la gates them, it does not derive them")(
  NILc))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))
glyph MAIN = print(REPORT)
